Software does not place independent code under this license.
"Licensor" means each copyright holder offering material under these terms,
solely to the extent of the rights that holder controls. "You" means the person
or legal entity exercising the permissions below. The project name does not
identify a separate legal entity or transfer ownership of anyone's contribution.

Subject to these terms, each Licensor grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide,
royalty-free copyright license, for the duration of the applicable copyright
unless terminated under section 6, to use, copy, study, modify and distribute the
Software and to make its functionality available remotely. Individuals and
organizations, including businesses, may use and modify it for their own work
and internal commercial purposes without a fee. Exercising permissions that
require this license constitutes acceptance of its conditions. Activities
permitted independently by law or another license do not require acceptance.

Internal use includes work by your employees and contractors acting solely on
your behalf and subject to these terms. Customers and other third parties do
not become internal users merely because you host their access on your servers.
Other legal entities must exercise their own rights under this license.

2. No sale or paid access

You may not sell, rent or charge a license, download or distribution fee for the
Software or any modified version. You may not distribute it as part of a paid
bundle or product, even if its price is not itemized separately. Copies must be
provided free of charge, without a required purchase, subscription or donation.

You may not use the Software to provide others with paid remote access to, or
paid use of, its functionality, whether directly or through a hosted service,
API, independent wrapper or modified version. This also applies when such access
is bundled into a paid offering or is available only to paying customers,
regardless of how the fee is named.
This restriction does not prohibit an organization from running the Software
on its own servers for its own internal work.

This restriction does not prohibit earning money from work performed using the
Software, including database administration and consulting, or charging for
optional support or training. Such charges must not be a condition of receiving
a copy of, a license to, or remote access to the Software. For example, a
consultant may charge for administering a customer's database while operating
the Software as a tool; that exception does not authorize selling the customer
access to the Software's functionality. Voluntary donations are permitted if
receiving the Software, remote access and its licensed rights does not depend
on donating.
Data, query results and other output are not covered merely because the Software
was used to create or process them.

3. Distribution and source code

When distributing the Software, including a modified version, you must:

(a) retain applicable copyright notices and provide this entire license;
(b) license your modifications to the Software under these same terms, without
    adding restrictions on the rights granted here;
(c) identify that you changed the Software if you distribute a modified version;
(d) provide the complete corresponding source code free of charge, either with
    each copy or through a clearly identified, working download made available
    to the same recipients for as long as you distribute or otherwise make that
    version available. For delivery without an ongoing download offering, include
    the corresponding source with the copy.
    For a public distribution, the corresponding source download must also be
    public and free of charge.

"Corresponding source" means the preferred form for making modifications to
that version, including its modifications and the build scripts needed to build
it. It does not include general-purpose tools or separately licensed components
that are not derived from the Software. Each recipient receives the permissions
in this license directly from the applicable copyright holders. You need not
publish changes kept solely for your own or your organization's internal use.

